{
  "_comment": "How an /authorize response is read, shared by the Python and TypeScript SDKs. Precedence: Quarantine / Terminate / SeverSubtree / Revoke first (a Quarantine whose payload is missing or malformed, or in the legacy flattened `details` shape, is still a quarantine that ends the run); then Deny + escalation_required (a literal true) + a non-empty approval_request_id, both under details or both at the top level, is needs_approval; then only a literal `allow` allows; everything else is deny. Checked by watchlight-core/tests/test_decision_precedence_fixture.py and watchlight-agent-sdk-ts/tests/decision-order.test.ts.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "allow",
      "response": {
        "decision": "Allow"
      },
      "kind": "allow"
    },
    {
      "name": "allow, any case",
      "response": {
        "decision": "allow"
      },
      "kind": "allow"
    },
    {
      "name": "a padded allow is not allow",
      "response": {
        "decision": " allow "
      },
      "kind": "deny"
    },
    {
      "name": "permit is not allow",
      "response": {
        "decision": "Permit"
      },
      "kind": "deny"
    },
    {
      "name": "deny",
      "response": {
        "decision": "Deny",
        "reason": "r"
      },
      "kind": "deny"
    },
    {
      "name": "missing decision",
      "response": {},
      "kind": "deny"
    },
    {
      "name": "unknown decision",
      "response": {
        "decision": "Maybe"
      },
      "kind": "deny"
    },
    {
      "name": "a bare NeedsApproval string is not a wl-apdp decision",
      "response": {
        "decision": "NeedsApproval"
      },
      "kind": "deny"
    },
    {
      "name": "deny + escalation + approval id (details)",
